course: dictionary
lesson: 1346
title: A place to camp
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A campsite is a place where people camp in tents, caravans or campervans. Read the clues: «Food, rubbish and even toothpaste must be stored away from bears at a campsite.» People stay outdoors there, so food and rubbish must be kept safe.
explain: Some campsites have toilets, showers and water taps, and some have none. «At a campsite without toilets, go with a grown-up at least 60 metres (about 200 feet) from water and bury it or pack it out.» So the word covers both busy, well-equipped sites and simple wild ones.
explain: The word can also mean the exact spot where one group puts up its tent. To check, swap in the word "place" and read the sentence again. In the US, a campsite is often called a campground.
fact: A campsite is a place where people camp in tents, caravans or campervans.
fact: Many campsites have toilets, showers and water taps, but some do not.
fact: A safe campsite is flat, away from rivers that might flood, and away from dead trees.
fact: Keep food sealed and stored away from animals, because «bears come to food smells at a campsite».
fact: Leave no trace: take your rubbish home and leave the campsite clean.
exercise: «Food, rubbish and even toothpaste must be stored away from bears at a campsite.» Where should food be kept to stay safe? | Scattered on the ground for the birds | Left open on the picnic table | *Sealed and stored away from animals
exercise: What is a campsite? | A kind of heavy metal ball for a game | A shop that sells camping gear | *A place where people camp in tents, caravans or campervans
exercise: Which spot is the safest for a tent on a campsite? | *A flat spot, away from rivers and dead trees | A spot right next to a river bank | At the bottom of a steep slope | Under a dead tree that could fall
test: Mum says, «Let's book a campsite near the lake.» What is she planning? | *To reserve a place to camp by the lake | To buy a new tent from a shop | To cook dinner at home | To swim across the lake
test: Dad says, «Our campsite is the flat grass by the gate.» What does campsite mean here? | *The exact spot where our tent goes | A school trip on a bus | A kind of rucksack | A map of the hills
exam: Which is a good campsite rule that keeps people and animals safe? | Leave rubbish next to the bins for the foxes | Feed the gulls from your hand | *Store your food sealed away from bears | Light a fire under a dead tree
